  "verbalization": "Retrofractamide C appears to interact with HPAC through a series of molecular targets, with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-8 acting as a central mediator. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including Butyl 2-(2,5-dihydroxyphenyl)acetate, Barringtogenol C, and Melafolone, all of which are linked to HPAC via a target-to-target relationship. The consistent presence of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-8 as a common intermediate suggests a potential mechanism where Retrofractamide C influences this enzyme, which in turn affects HPAC. The evidence supports a pathway where Retrofractamide C may modulate the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-8, potentially altering the metabolic processing of substrates that ultimately interact with HPAC. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Retrofractamide C in regulating the enzyme activity that leads to HPAC engagement, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
